> If you're using [LiteLLM](https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/issues/21998#issuecomment-3991509362), adding a separate provider for OpenAI models (GPT-5.4) pointing at `@ai-sdk/openai` rather than `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` should resolve the issue:
> 
> {
>   "provider": {
>     "my-litellm-provider": {
>       "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
>       "options": {
>         "baseURL": "https://my-provider.url/api/v1"
>       },
>       "models": {
>         ...
>       }
>     },
>     "my-litellm-provider-openai": {
>       "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai",
>       "options": {
>         "baseURL": "https://my-provider.url/api/v1"
>       },
>       "models": {
>         ...
>       }
>     }
>   }
> }

